# The decoder's entry point.
#
# Protocol: stdin gives the input path and the output path (natively
# `/file/<absolute path>`), and optionally a third line: `nosmooth` selects
# plain replication of subsampled components, as `djpeg -nosmooth`; anything
# else, or no third line, selects fancy (triangle) upsampling, as default
# djpeg. stdout gets `FRAME width height ncomp kind`, then `DECODED`, with
# the image written to the output path as djpeg writes it: P5 for greyscale,
# P6 otherwise, CMYK and YCCK converted to RGB; maxval 255, or 4095 with two
# big-endian bytes a sample for a 12-bit frame; the exit status is 0. A
# refusal is a trap `REFUSED CODE: message` on stderr with exit status 1; any
# other trap is a decoder bug. The output is opened before decoding, so a
# refusal mid-scan can leave a partial file holding the rows flushed so far,
# in whole 1 MiB buffers: the harness ignores it, and the service deletes the
# request directory.

: main ( -- )
  read-line drop :> inp
  read-line drop :> outp
  read-line drop :> mode
  inp source.load markers.open :> j
  j markers.walk
  j huffman.scan-tables :> tabs
  j markers.frame-line println
  j tabs  mode "nosmooth" str.eq i32.eqz  rows.setup :> d
  outp d decoder.width d decoder.height d decoder.ncomp d decoder.f frame.precision ppm.open :> p
  d [ ( bytes -- ) p swap ppm.row ] rows.decode
  p out.close
  "DECODED" println ;
